{* Every dialog the app adds: a header band, a body that scrolls, a footer band with the actions,
	around one POST form. Used with {embed}, filling the slots:

		{embed '../Assets/modal.latte', id: 'my-dialog', class: 'my-dialog', close: $desktop->t('modal.close')}
			{block hidden}{input_token()|noescape}{/block}
			{block header}<h2>Title</h2>{/block}
			{block body}…fields…{/block}
			{block footer}<button class="ad-primary">Save</button>{/block}
		{/embed}

	The look is css/modal.css. Buttons in the footer are quiet unless they take .ad-primary (the
	one green action, last) or .ad-danger (outlined red, pushed to the left).

	The way out is the × in the header's top-right corner, on every modal; close is its translated
	name, passed in because an embedded template sees only what it is given. So the footer carries
	no Close of its own — only a question does, as its safe answer beside the destructive one.

	Every way out — Escape, a click outside (lightDismiss), the ×, any button with data-close — is
	one close request, and with guard on, a changed form asks before it is discarded
	(javascript/modal.js).
	A button with data-dialog="<id>" anywhere on the page opens it.

	form: false for a modal that sits inside a form it belongs to — adminer's login form, whose
	fields have to post with it — since a form cannot hold another. labelledBy names the element
	in the header that gives the dialog its accessible name; label names it outright, for a header
	with no heading to point at. focusSelf puts the focus on the dialog when it opens, for one whose
	first focusable element is not where the user starts. *}
{parameters
	string $id,
	string $close,
	string $class = '',
	bool $lightDismiss = true,
	bool $guard = false,
	bool $form = true,
	string $labelledBy = '',
	string $label = '',
	bool $focusSelf = false
}
<dialog id="{$id}" class="ad-modal {$class}" n:attr="closedby: $lightDismiss ? 'any', data-guard: $guard, aria-labelledby: $labelledBy ?: null, aria-label: $label ?: null, tabindex: $focusSelf ? -1 : null, data-focus-self: $focusSelf">
	<form n:tag-if="$form" action="" method="post">
		{block hidden}{/block}
		<div class="ad-modal-header">
			{block header}{/block}
			{* Named by aria-label alone: a title saying the same would be read out a second time, as
				the button's description. *}
			<button type="button" class="ad-modal-close" data-close aria-label="{$close}">
				<svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3.5 3.5l9 9m0-9l-9 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
			</button>
		</div>
		<div class="ad-modal-body">{block body}{/block}</div>
		<div class="ad-modal-footer">{block footer}{/block}</div>
	</form>
</dialog>
